	<ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-70" contextRef="c-00">6. Refer to Notes to the Financial Statement, Section 11, Debt.</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
	<ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-71" contextRef="c-00">7. Chugach Electric Association's annual membership meeting was held on May 30, 2025. In this year's election, Chugach members approved one bylaw amendment: The amendment allows the cooperative to hold its annual meeting between April 15 and June 15 in a given year.</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
	<ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-72" contextRef="c-00">8. Chugach has three Collective Bargaining Agreements (CBA's) with the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers (IBEW), representing approximately 75% of its workforce. Chugach also has a CBA with the Hotel Employees &amp; Restaurant Employees (HERE) union. All three IBEW CBA's were negotiated with a new expiration date of June 30th, 2028. Effective July 1, 2025, new wage tables went into effect as bargained and agreed to for all IBEW employees, which included a 8% increase in base wages for all three IBEW CBAs. Future wage increases and health and welfare premium cost sharing provisions are outlined annually for the remaining years of the existing IBEW CBA's. The HERE CBA was negotiated with a new expiration date of June 30, 2028, and a base wage increase of $1.25 effective July 1, 2025. Future wage increases are outlined annually for the remaining years of the existing HERE CBA.</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
	<ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-73" contextRef="c-00">9. Refer to Notes to the Financial Statement, Section 5, Regulatory Matters and Section 18, Commitments and Contingencies.</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
	<ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-74" contextRef="c-00">13. Our Annual meeting was held on May 30, 2025 at ChangePoint Alaska, where Katherine Jernstrom was elected. Election of the officers was held at the May 30, 2025, Regular Board Meeting, with the following results: Mark Wiggin - Board Chair, Sisi Cooper - Board Vice Chair, Susanne Fleek-Green - Board Secretary, Rachel Morse - Board Treasurer, Jim Nordlund - Board Director, Daniel Rogers - Board Director, Katherine Jernstrom - Newly elected Board Director.</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
